
==============================================================================
(G) Proposition 5.4: exact probability that the coin's run law lies in M_N (human = random function)
==============================================================================
  u= 6 N=2 delta=0.50: Pr[Q_coin in M_N] = 0.9861 >= 1 - delta - C(N,2)/u = 0.3333 : True
  u= 8 N=3 delta=0.30: Pr[Q_coin in M_N] = 0.9785 >= 1 - delta - C(N,2)/u = 0.3250 : True
  u=10 N=2 delta=0.20: Pr[Q_coin in M_N] = 0.9950 >= 1 - delta - C(N,2)/u = 0.7000 : True
  u= 5 N=3 delta=0.60: Pr[Q_coin in M_N] = 0.9480 >= 1 - delta - C(N,2)/u = -0.2000 : True

==============================================================================
(H) Proposition 6.4: the collision statistic
==============================================================================
  2000 random pairs of laws on q<=6 answers: max |E[s|x] - d(x)^2| = 6.66e-16; -1/2 <= s <= 2: True
  s = -1/2 attained (A = (1/2,1/2,0..), y1 != y2 in its support): -0.500; s = 2 approached (A concentrated on y' != y1 = y2): 2.000
  (b) with m=150, delta=0.10: fraction of 3000 trials with D2 > sbar + (5/2)sqrt(ln(1/delta)/(2m)) = 0.0000 (<= delta)
  (c) beta <= (L/2)sqrt(q D2) on 10 random toy scaffolds: True
  binary answers: sum (P-A)^2 = 2 TV^2: True

